# Same range cuts as the DC3/DC4 sources (optimizes sim time):
DefaultRangeCut 0.005
Region Spacecraft
Spacecraft.Volume SCbody
Spacecraft.RangeCut 1.

Region Pipebody
Pipebody.Volume PIPbody
Pipebody.RangeCut 1.

DetectorTimeConstant 0.000002

# Distant particle event: bremsstrahlung from electrons (exp(-E/500 keV)) precipitating
# over 90000 km2 at 10 deg Earth-central angle (1272 km away, zenith 119.5 deg,
# azimuth 270 deg from north). Peak precipitating flux 9.2e+03 e/cm2/s above 50 keV.
# Peak photon flux at COSI 0.255 ph/cm2/s; Flux below is the lightcurve-averaged value.
# Rocking -21.88 deg, yaw -39.31 deg. Direction in detector frame.
DataChallenge.Source E_DISTPAR0044
E_DISTPAR0044.ParticleType 1
E_DISTPAR0044.Beam FarFieldGaussian 117.222 62.612 6.759
E_DISTPAR0044.Spectrum File E_DISTPAR0044_spectrum.dat
E_DISTPAR0044.Flux 0.0703995
# Light-curve times are relative to t_ref = 1835752305.0 (unix s, first orientation row of this burst).
# Simulate with DC3_final_530km_3_month_with_slew_15sbins_GalacticEarth_cut_normed.ori and add t_ref to the simulated times afterwards.
# Original light curve (absolute unix times): E_DISTPAR0044_lightcurve.dat; see sim_time_reference.txt.
E_DISTPAR0044.Lightcurve File false E_DISTPAR0044_lightcurve_shifted.dat
E_DISTPAR0044.EarthOccultation false
